<h4 align="center">&nbsp;Angel Tree</h4>
<p>Each year, The Salvation Army of Augusta’s Angel Tree Program ensures that local children experiencing financial hardship wake up to gifts, clothing, and essentials on Christmas morning. This year, we are honored to serve about 500 families — representing more than 1,200 children across the Augusta area. Your generosity makes this possible.</p>
<p></p>
<h5>How to Adopt an Angel</h5>
<p>Angel Tree tags list a child’s age, clothing sizes, needs, and holiday wish list. You can select a tag in person or shop <a href="https://www.walmart.com/registry/RR/e550f2c6-3fa0-4bab-86c7-216302b0c88f" target="">online</a>.</p>
<p><span data-teams="true">More info about where to adopt an Angel will be available in November.&nbsp;</span></p>
<ul></ul>
<p><strong>Prefer to give from home?</strong> You can purchase gifts directly through our Walmart Angel Tree Registry, and items will ship straight to us.</p>
<p class="cta-button-group d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 my-3 justify-content-center" style="text-align: center;"><a class="btn btn-secondary gap-1 mt-2" href="https://www.walmart.com/registry/RR/e550f2c6-3fa0-4bab-86c7-216302b0c88f">Shop online</a></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"></p>
<h5>Gift Drop-Off Information</h5>
<p><u><strong>All Angel Tree gifts must be dropped off at The Salvation Army Kroc Center (1833 Broad Street, Augusta, GA). Please return gifts unwrapped and with their Angel tag attached.</strong></u></p>
<p></p>
<h5>Volunteer with Angel Tree</h5>
<p>Behind the scenes, dozens of volunteers help sort gifts and prepare for our distribution day. We invite you to give the gift of your time this Christmas. Volunteers are needed for gift sorting and prep, as well as support on Distribution Day. Click the button below to register.</p>
<p class="cta-button-group d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 my-3 justify-content-center" style="text-align: center;"><a class="btn btn-secondary gap-1 mt-2" href="https://salvationarmyaugusta.galaxydigital.com/agency/detail/angeltree/?agency_id=158175">Volunteer</a></p>
</div></div>
